1. She earned a Master's degree and considered pursuing a PhD, ultimately graduating top of her class. (Verbatim: "I took mine all the way to PhD. No, actually, I started thinking about that kind of thing when I was doing my Masters... I graduated top of my class.")

2. During her Master's program, she learned the importance of taking breaks and not overworking herself, a shift from her earlier mindset of viewing breaks as wasted time. (Verbatim: "I used to never give myself any mental health time or breaks or anything because I'd be like time wasted on breaks is time I couldn't use studying.")

3. She played Stardew Valley extensively during her Master's studies as a way to relax, even playing for 24 hours straight without guilt. (Verbatim: "I remember finally freeing myself of that guilt where I could play Stardew Valley for like 24 hours when I should have been studying... I played a lot of Stardew during my Masters.")

4. Her mother, referred to as "Mama Elia," worked long hours and prioritized her job over family, which made a strong impression on her and influenced her views on work-life balance. (Verbatim: "Mama Elia would always be like oh sorry I can't do this for you my work needs me... it makes me sad that her work made her feel that way.")

5. Mama Elia worked as a cashier but took on managerial responsibilities without the title or pay, a situation that has persisted for as long as she can remember. (Verbatim: "She's still like that she still does that she still will drop everything for her work... she basically does all the work that a manager should do.")

6. She has a habit of apologizing frequently, which she traces back to being told to be quiet or "shut up" by Papa Elia whenever she made noise as a child. (Verbatim: "I just remember being told to shut up by papa elia so... actually no that was with any noise I made so maybe that's why I'm so used to saying sorry.")

7. She does not possess the photic sneeze reflex (the ability to sneeze when looking at bright light), and mentions that only about one-third of people have the gene for it. (Verbatim: "I've never that that's never helped me... I believe there is a specific gene for that trigger so those that it does work for it really does work for.")

8. She made a personal promise to work less, enjoy life more, and prioritize happiness and self-care over overwork. (Verbatim: "I also made a promise to go out and enjoy more and do more projects and stay happy and work way less.")

9. She speaks some Japanese and Korean, using phrases like "arigato" and "Annyeong" during the stream. (Verbatim: "Annyeong! Annyeong! Annyeong!" and "arigato control these nuts")

10. She jokes about her mind being a place where fans live rent-free, referring to herself as a "kind landlord" and expressing deep appreciation for her community. (Verbatim: "You don't... You all get to live in my brain rent-free, you know that, right? I am a very kind landlord.") [end of text]



1. She has knowledge of British cultural customs, specifically the use of "x" to mean "kiss" in messages. (Verbatim: "Yeah, ex, the little 'x' symbol means 'kiss' in, um, in England. Yeah, it's a British thing to put it on the end of messages.")

